Heart failure is most often characterized as systolic, if[ eject]ion fraction (EF) is decreased, and diastolic, if[ eject]ion fraction is preserved.[ �]�Diastolic[�]� heart failure is also often called heart failure with preserved[ eject]ion fraction ([H]FPEF) or heart failure with preserved[ sy]stolic function ([HF]PSF).
